      "type": "logic_error / governance threshold manipulation via dynamic totalSupply",
      "severity": "medium",
      "vulnerable_function": "currentTokenSupply()",
      "location": "LockToVotePlugin.currentTokenSupply",
      "explanation": "The plugin uses currentTokenSupply() = IERC20(lockManager.token()).totalSupply() as the denominator for governance threshold checks (e.g., minimum participation / approval). For tokens whose totalSupply can be changed permissionlessly or via flash mechanisms (ERC4626 share tokens via deposit/withdraw, flash-mintable tokens, rebasing/mintable tokens), an attacker can temporarily inflate (or deflate) totalSupply at the moment thresholds are evaluated. Because proposal tallies are based on locked voting power while the denominator is live totalSupply, a transient supply change can skew ratios without the attacker needing corresponding locked voting power. This breaks the invariant that thresholds reflect the electorate that can actually vote/lock, and enables last-block outcome manipulation.",
      "attack_scenario": "1) A proposal is near the minimum participation/approval threshold near the end of voting.\n2) Attacker uses a flash-mint (or ERC4626 deposit that mints many shares) to temporarily increase token totalSupply for the block when execution/validation occurs.\n3) currentTokenSupply() returns the inflated supply.\n4) Threshold checks compute (tally / inflatedSupply), making participation/approval appear lower.\n5) Proposal that would otherwise pass is made to fail; attacker then reverses the mint/burn/withdraw in the same transaction (or shortly after), making the manipulation effectively risk-free aside from fees.",
      "suggested_fix": "Snapshot the supply used for thresholds at proposal creation (or at startDate), and use that stored value for all later threshold checks.\nExample: store proposal_.snapshotSupply = IERC20(token).totalSupply() in createProposal, and have currentTokenSupply() (or threshold logic) read proposal_.snapshotSupply. Alternatively, enforce/token-gate to non-flash-mintable, non-permissionless-mint tokens and document compatibility."
    }
  ],
  "overall_explanation": "LockToVotePlugin implements majority voting where tallies come from locked balances tracked by a LockManager, while threshold logic relies on currentTokenSupply(). Because currentTokenSupply reads live ERC20 totalSupply, any token with manipulable supply enables risk-free, last-block governance threshold manipulation. No trusted role compromise is required—only access to supply-changing mechanics of the underlying token."
